# Streets close into a square of the road grid: road laid on towards a street
# crossing its way runs across it at its crossroads place, and the two meet
# there at a crossroads of their own.
> new empty
> free on
> construction off
> build crossroads at s0:55
  #1 intersection at s0:55-57, done
> build crossroads at s0:82
  #3 intersection at s0:82-84, done
> ride s1:135
  rider: s1:135 facing +
> lay road 3
  s1 now runs cells 127..216
> ride s2:135
  rider: s2:135 facing +
> lay road 3
  s2 now runs cells 127..216
> build crossroads at s1:157
  #13 intersection at s1:157-159, done
> expect streets 4
  ok: 4 streets
# the other corner of the square is on the line s3 runs along: s3 is laid on to it instead
> expect cannot build crossroads at s2:157 lay its road on to here
  ok: can't build intersection at s2:157: A street runs along this line already: lay its road on to here
> ride s3:131
  rider: s3:131 facing +
> lay road 1 start
  s3 now runs cells 100..135
> streets
  s0  runs east (lots on its north side), cells 16..246
  s1  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 127..216, from crossroads #1
  s2  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 127..216, from crossroads #3
  s3  runs west (lots on its south side), cells 100..135, from crossroads #13
    crossroads #1: s0:56 = s1:131 (cell A56)
    crossroads #3: s0:83 = s2:131 (cell A83)
    crossroads #13: s1:158 = s3:131 (cell AB56)
    crossroads #17: s2:158 = s3:104 (cell AB83)
> expect streets 4
  ok: 4 streets
